    "narrative": "For today\u2019s matchup, **Yordan Alvarez** (77.62) and **Christian Yelich** (74.32) headline our offensive output, serving as the core of the Zurich Zebras\u2019 lineup. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start due to his elite 0.448 xwOBA, while **Christian Yelich** draws a highly favorable matchup against Elder, where a combination of a +13% platoon edge and the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery significantly boosts his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of the scarce SB category. **Kyle Schwarber** (67.41) and **Trea Turner** (67.08) follow closely behind; despite **Trea Turner** facing a tough catcher with a 1.87s pop time, his leadoff spot and favorable dynamic platoon numbers make him an essential engine for run production today.\n\nWe are navigating several tactical edges to maximize our efficiency. **Casey Schmitt** (62.41) is a strong start at 1B, benefiting from an exploitable SP skill set and a slow delivery from Gusto that favors our baserunning profile. Meanwhile, **Lars Nootbaar** (64.37) earns a spot thanks to a wind-out forecast and a solid +11% platoon bump. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Caleb Durbin** (41.23); while he offers speed, his matchup against the elite Logan Gilbert necessitated a stay on the bench, as his efficiency rating dropped below our threshold compared to the high-ceiling options currently slated in the utility and infield slots. \n\nRisk management remains a priority for the rotation. We are monitoring **Carson Benge** (45.89) closely, as he draws Wheeler\u2014an elite arm who drastically suppressed his projected score\u2014and we must be prepared to pinch-hit if the matchup proves too restrictive. Additionally, the rainout for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** provides a forced day of rest, and we continue to track **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds**, who remain in the minors and unavailable for selection. Managers should note that while **Dillon Dingler** (45.20) and **Junior Caminero** (54.78) sit toward the bottom of our active recommendations, their platoon advantages keep them narrowly ahead of our deep bench alternatives.",
